# Kanban feature cards

When frontmatter is **`labels: ["feature"]`** (inline JSON array — required form), follow [kanban-markdown/SKILL.md](../skills/kanban-markdown/SKILL.md) § Feature cards.

**Do not** use empty `labels: []` — that is **invalid**; stop and ask the user to set `labels: ["feature"]` ([agent-routing.mdc](agent-routing.mdc) § Card label gate).

## Frontmatter (required on create)

```yaml
labels: ["feature"]
```

## User provides

- Story / summary, **`## Feature Areas`**, **`## Acceptance Criteria`** (behavior draft or agent completes)
- **`## Verify`** (optional — manual app checks)

## Agent provides (pre-implementation card review)

- **`## Product Paths`** — product code from Feature Areas via `docs/feature-areas.yaml` (no `tests/`)
- **`## Product Methods`** — symbols to edit (when Feature Areas set)
- **`## Tests`** — **Files**, **Methods**, **Verify (agent)** — see [reference.md § Tests](../skills/kanban-markdown/reference.md#tests)
- **`## Docs`** — doc paths + § hints from area `docs:`
- **`## Decisions`** — concrete plan before `in-progress`
- **`## Acceptance Criteria`** — behavior-only bullets `[ ]` when missing (no pytest paths or `test_*`)

**Legacy alias:** cards under `done/` / `archived/` may use **Label Paths** / **Label Methods** — parsers
read as Product (Signature: `kanban-card-scope-schema`).

## Card Done — lessons learned (mandatory)

When the user signals **QA-complete / Done**, the **agent** moves the card to `done/` and runs
Card Done **same turn** (Signature: `card-done-agent-move-qa-complete`):

1. Run [kanban-markdown/SKILL.md](../skills/kanban-markdown/SKILL.md) § Card Done — lessons learned capture.
2. Update **≥1 skill** + **≥1 rule** + relevant **`docs/`** / registry.
3. Add **`## Lessons captured (YYYY-MM-DD)`** on the card.
4. Add **`## Forward-looking feedback (YYYY-MM-DD)`** after Lessons captured (Signature:
   `card-done-forward-feedback` — [reference.md](../skills/kanban-markdown/reference.md)
   § Forward-looking feedback: Impact Scope, References, Mitigation on max tier, Importance
   when tied; top-3 in chat on Card Done turn).

**Do not** skip lessons capture because AC were already `[x]`.

## Workflow

1. Confirm **`labels: ["feature"]`** and user story / Feature Areas present
2. Resolve Feature Areas → **Product Paths** + **Product Methods** + **Tests** + **Docs**
3. Prior lessons gate → refresh **Context** / **Decisions** card links (`archived/` / `done/`; mark closed deps) → **Decisions** → `todo` → `in-progress` → implement
4. **Tests** complete — draft **Tests → Files** from Product Paths via
   `python3 scripts/resolve_card_tests.py --from-card CARD.md --files-only`; stage paths;
   `scripts/pre-commit-pytest.sh` or `scripts/agent-commit-ready.sh` green; cross-check card **Tests →
   Files** vs hook output (Signature: `precommit-pytest-scope-mismatch`); `docs/feature-areas.yaml` +
   card **Docs** paths updated per [docs-maintenance](../skills/docs-maintenance/SKILL.md)
5. Mark AC `[x]` → `review` → user Verify / QA
6. User **QA-complete / Done** → agent moves to `done/` + lessons learned (not optional)

## Do not

- Use **`## Corrective Action`** or **`## Response`** on feature cards
- Implement without an assigned kanban card ([agent-routing.mdc](agent-routing.mdc))
- Leave **`## Decisions`** as `TBD` before `in-progress`
- Skip **Product Methods** / **Tests** / **Docs** when Feature Areas are set — complete before **Review**
- Put pytest commands or `test_*` names in **Acceptance Criteria** — use **Tests**
- **Superseded GovernanceDriftAlert siblings** — when fix landed on a parent `done/` card (same `_SCHEMA_INTERNAL_PATHS` / shared root cause), update sibling with **Decisions** `Superseded` + link, AC `[x]`, `review`; close without re-implementing — cite parent **Lessons captured** (kanban-markdown reference § Card Done artifact table)
- **GovernanceDriftAlert batch (2026-06-28)** — group spawns by root cause: (1) extend `_SCHEMA_INTERNAL_PATHS` for `docs/governance/*` + hook scripts, (2) add `agent-triage/reference.md` § Lessons by area rows for seeded `lesson_signatures`, (3) dedupe cross-area `handlers:`, (4) register kanban Product Methods on yaml — one anchor card with **Lessons captured**; siblings **Superseded** — Signature: `governance-area-schema-parity-tests`
- **GovernanceDriftAlert epic closed 2026-06-29** — do not reuse `epic:` on new cards; use a new PascalCase epic for drift follow-ups — [docs/epics-closed.yaml](../../docs/epics-closed.yaml)
- **Parity spawn (GovernanceDriftFix)** — `check_governance_parity.py` consolidates alerts by root
