## Floating Camera keyboard movement

When **Feature Areas** include **`Floating Camera`** or AC describes 3D orbit keyboard fly
(`WASD`, Space, Shift), include a behavior AC bullet:

- Hold movement keys move continuously until release (not tap-only per `keyPressEvent`)

Signature: `floating-camera-fc0-hold-fly`. Parent ff: `ff-feature-floating-camera-reset-fc1-2026-06-28-governance-01-4ba51333`.

**Hold-fly implementation:** `keyReleaseEvent` must ignore `event.isAutoRepeat()` (mirror
`keyPressEvent`) — auto-repeat releases clear `_held_movement_keys` and stop movement after one step.

## Floating Camera look-direction forward (fc1b)

When AC covers W/S/↑/↓ along the look vector:

- Wire forward/back via `move_along_look`; strafe via `move_on_plane(..., forward_delta=0, ...)`
- Pitched-down unit test before widget wiring (`test_move_along_look_follows_pitch_when_elevation_nonzero`)

Signature: `floating-camera-fc1b-look-forward`.

## Floating Camera pose persistence (fc1c)

When AC covers saving 3D orbit camera pose across sessions:

- Store under `viewer.orbit_camera_poses` keyed `{structure}/{stage}` (not one global triple)
- `PreviewPanel.set_orbit_pose_scope(structure, stage)` before save/restore
- Call `_persist_editor_settings()` before `open_structure_in_editor_process` / `_restart_editor_for_structure` (`execve` skips `closeEvent`)
- Manual QA: stage A → stage B → stage A via **Open Recent** with **3D** poses on each

Signature: `floating-camera-fc1c-pose-persistence`. Parent ff:
`ff-feature-floating-camera-pose-persistence-fc1c-2026-06-29-governance-01`.

## Floating Camera orientation HUD (fc3)

When **Feature Areas** include **`Floating Camera`** and AC covers the 3-line HUD:

- Top-right QLabel; pref `viewer.orbit_camera_hud` (default on); **Viewer → Camera HUD** (3D only)
- `format_hud_block_label` → `format_entry_label` for materialized catalog names (Oak Log, not Log)
- Full-cell `raycast_voxel` + `hud_voxel_map` is acceptable for fc3 ship; perceived geometry false hits
  on attachables/partial blocks → **validate with fc3a crosshair first** — bug a8e closed Done 2026-06-29
  (Looking at correct; no geometry raycast). Reopen only if crosshair-aligned QA still fails.
  Signature: `floating-camera-fc3-orientation-hud`, `floating-camera-fc3a-crosshair`.

## Floating Camera HUD crosshair (fc3a)

When AC covers the center-screen look-ray reticle:

- Qt overlay `_CrosshairOverlay` on `OrbitPreviewWidget` — **not** GL draw calls
- White dot + four gap-separated arms; `_layout_crosshair()` centers on widget resize
- `WA_TransparentForMouseEvents`; same visibility gate as HUD (`_hud_overlay_visible`)
- `PreviewPanel.set_orbit_view_active` / `set_orbit_view_active(False)` on **2D** toggle
- **Click-to-capture (fc3a QA):** `_capture_pointer()` → `grabMouse()` + `grabKeyboard()` + `BlankCursor`;
  mouse deltas from **global** position so look continues outside widget bounds; **Esc** / focus-out /
  **2D** toggle → `_release_pointer()`; no auto-focus on **3D** entry
- Independent crosshair pref deferred to fc3b — follows **Viewer → Camera HUD** until then
- Offscreen pytest: simulate `focusInEvent`/`focusOutEvent` — `QOpenGLWidget.setFocus()` may fail without GL

Signature: `floating-camera-fc3a-crosshair`. Blocks fc3b **Show Crosshairs** checkbox.

## Floating Camera mouse look (fc2a)

When AC covers pointer look without click-drag:

- **`setMouseTracking(True)`** on `OrbitPreviewWidget` — Qt omits `mouseMoveEvent` without tracking
- Gate look on widget **`hasFocus()`** (click 3D view to capture); **fc3a QA:** not hover-only
- **`BlankCursor`** via `QApplication.setOverrideCursor` while focused; restore on focus-out
- **Esc** → `clearFocus()` restores cursor and stops look
- Do **not** auto-focus orbit widget on **3D** tab entry — user clicks to capture
- Reset `_last_look_pos` via `_reset_mouse_look_anchor` on focus-in; suppress first-move snap
- Remove 3D `wheelEvent` dolly; **2D** Viewer zoom menu unchanged
- Scroll → movement speed is **fc2b** — unblocked after fc2a Done
- **Review QA:** assert focus-gate + Esc cursor tests before manual pointer-look QA

Signature: `floating-camera-fc2a-mouse-look`. Depends: fc0/fc1b keyboard paths unchanged.

## Floating Camera scroll move speed (fc2b)

When AC covers scroll → keyboard fly speed:

- **3D** scroll or **+** / **-** adjusts `viewer.orbit_camera_move_speed` (±0.1/step; clamp **0.25–4.0**; default **0.65×**); no camera dolly; mouse look sensitivity **unchanged**
- Gate wheel on `hasFocus()` or `_pointer_captured` (same as fc2a capture path)
- Speed label on **`_OrbitViewHost`** sibling in `preview_panel.py` — orbit `move_speed_feedback` signal;
  **not** child QLabel on QOpenGLWidget; **never** QPainter in `paintGL`
- Scale **`_movement_speed_per_second()`** / **`_movement_distance(elapsed_ms)`** on timer tick — not fixed step per 50 ms; 16 ms tick + `QElapsedTimer` (fc2b QA smoothness at low multiplier)
- Transient **Move speed: N.N×** label below crosshair (~1.5s `QTimer` hide); not permanent HUD line
- Overlay hint mentions scroll; **2D** preview wheel unchanged
- Pref round-trip via `ui/app_settings.py` + `ui/editor_prefs.py` + `config/editor_settings.yaml`

Signature: `floating-camera-fc2b-scroll-move-speed`. Depends: fc2a removed scroll dolly.

## Floating Camera HUD settings (fc3b)

When AC covers HUD Properties modal:

- **Viewer → HUD Panel** (+ HUD cog) opens `CameraHudSettingsDialog`; **F3** toggles HUD panel (same as
  **Show HUD panel** / **HUD Panel** menu)
- Modal: placement (9 positions), **Show Crosshairs**, **Movement Speed** slider **0.2×–1.0×** (default **0.65×**)
- fc3b narrows fc2b speed clamp and sets scroll/key step **±0.05** (was ±0.1, max 4.0×)
- `_OrbitViewHost` speed label unchanged — modal + scroll share `viewer.orbit_camera_move_speed`

Signature: `floating-camera-fc3b-hud-settings`. Depends: fc3/fc3a/fc2b done.

